  "worked_solution": "Notice that the $4$th column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $4$th column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(E) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4} & \\frac{3}{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 6 & -5 & -\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{2}{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{8}{3} & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-1)^{1+4}|\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}| & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (6\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3})=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(E)=-2.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
